{"arrangement": "Claude Code 2.1.261 on macOS, eight arms, each its own session and its own capture directory. Hooks were installed project-locally in a scratch directory, never in the operator's settings, so nothing here could fire for another session. Interactive arms ran under tmux 3.7c on a socket this recorder mints, and the first-run trust prompt was answered as part of starting the session rather than measured.", "at": "2026-09-06T08:55:59Z", "format": 1, "not_measured": ["Any harness other than Claude Code.", "Any platform other than macOS.", "Power loss, an OOM kill, and a system shutdown, none of which were run. A SIGKILL is the nearest measured proxy for the first two.", "Whether a `reason` value beyond these two exists: /clear and logout were not driven, and the vocabulary is closed but not enumerated."], "note": true, "turn_open_at_end_caveat": "Three terminal-closed arms were driven with a prompt in flight and only a5c had the turn still open at the kill; a5 and a5b had a Stop arrive first, which their own records show. a2 and a3 were both genuinely mid-turn, so the mid-turn case is covered for the signal question by the signal arms rather than by the terminal arms.", "why_every_arm_records_session_started_observed": "The first run of the interactive arms parked on that trust prompt, so the session never started and the recorder saw no events at all. Read without the gate that is indistinguishable from a silent death, and would have produced exactly the wrong verdict. An arm proves nothing unless a SessionStart was observed for it.", "why_reason_separates_clean_from_killed_is_null": "Because it is neither true nor false as asked. `prompt_input_exit` is distinctive and means a deliberate quit inside the session. `other` is not: it covers a headless run that completed normally AND a SIGTERM AND a closed terminal. So the field separates one deliberate ending from everything else, and does not separate a clean ending from a killed one. A boolean here would assert more than the arms support."}
